  <h2>How Agent Shipping Insurance Works</h2>
  <p>
    When you finalize a parcel checkout on Kakobuy, you are offered an optional checkbox to purchase shipping insurance (usually costing around 2.5% to 4% of your total declared parcel value plus international shipping fees). 
  </p>
  <p>
    Many beginners mistakenly believe that insurance only covers physical damage or lost mail. On premium agent lines, however, high-value insurance policies cover <strong>customs seizures</strong> (customs confiscation) in both the export and import countries. If customs holds your package, or if it vanishes in transit, you are eligible for a full or partial refund of both the item cost and the shipping fees.
  </p>

  <h2>Decoding Seizure Compensation Tiers</h2>
  <p>
    When you build a haul from a trusted <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> directory and prepare to ship, you must analyze the insurance options available for your selected route:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Full Cover (Seizure + Lost + Damage):</strong> The gold standard. If customs destroys or retains your package due to intellectual property (IP) reasons, the agent refunds 100% of the declared item costs and 100% of the international shipping freight fees.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Standard Cover (Lost Only):</strong> Only covers scenarios where the parcel is officially declared "lost" by the postal carrier (e.g., tracking stops updating for over 60 days). It does <em>not</em> cover customs seizures. Avoid this tier if your haul contains restricted goods.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No-Cover Lines:</strong> Some ultra-budget postal lines do not offer any insurance. Shipping high-value branded garments or shoes via these routes is a massive gamble.
    </li>
  </ul>

