  <h2>How to File a Successful Claim: The Golden Rules</h2>
  <p>
    If the worst happens and your parcel is held, getting compensated requires following precise steps:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Do Not Panic:</strong> Customs inspection clearances can occasionally take up to 10 business days. Wait for an official update.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Obtain Written Proof:</strong> If seized, your local postal service or customs agency will mail you a seizure letter (confiscation notice). <em>Keep this document!</em> Kakobuy's insurance department requires a photo of this letter to verify the seizure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Submit Within the Window:</strong> Most insurance policies require you to file your claim within 7 to 30 days of the official transit freeze or seizure letter date. Submit the claim directly through your parcel console.
    </li>
  </ol>

